{"step_index":10056,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:06:25Z","thinking":"The `#progress-modal`'s absolute positioning and high `z-index` combined with its placement directly within the main content area create an overlay effect. This means when the modal is displayed, it covers the entire visible area of the main content. This is likely the cause of the reported issue, where clicking on other interface elements doesn't register while the progress modal is active.\n\n\nPlacing the progress modal within a specific screen container, instead of the main content area, would resolve the overlay issue. Applying absolute positioning to the modal within this container will confine its effect to that screen only. This approach ensures other screens remain accessible while the modal is active.\n\n\nThe error 429 indicates a concurrency limit, suggesting the server is overwhelmed by requests. The code uses a thread pool to process multiple files in parallel; this likely triggered the limit. Reducing the maximum number of parallel workers might resolve the issue.\n\n\nThe concurrent processing of files led to a concurrency limit error, indicating the server couldn't handle the simultaneous requests. The error occurred because the Google AI Studio uses only ONE browser tab. The thread pool design likely caused the server overload. Limiting the number of parallel threads seems a probable solution.\n\n\nThe successful processing of one PDF confirms the prompt and image transmission to the browser. The failures of the other files are due to concurrent processing through the thread pool overloading a single browser tab, exceeding its capacity. The error stemmed from the user terminating the server due to observed failures. The new process and cache directory confirm the system isn't using an old cache.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy-vision\\\\src\\\\extract\\\\file_handler.py\"","EndLine":"115","StartLine":"60","toolAction":"\"Viewing read_input_files in file_handler.py\"","toolSummary":"\"View read_input_files threading logic\""}}]}
